Three cheers for Ptolemy.  He was a great astronomer and mathematician of his time.

And for those who say he was "very wrong", I'd like to point out that, given the nature of scientific "progress", every great scientist of our time will be "very wrong" when looked at from the standpoint of some future scientist.

